// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PATCH LAYER — WordNet sentence frames 22 and 23 reclassified, WHOLE LEXICON.
//
// `convert.rs::classify` maps  1|2|3|22 => Intransitive and 4|12|23|27 => PpOblique, but
// `doc/man/wninput.5` says 22 is "Somebody ----s PP" (a PP frame) and 23 is
// "Somebody's (body part) ----s" (an intransitive). They are SWAPPED, so 22's PP is dropped and
// 23 gets a spurious oblique slot. Confirmed on one synset in 181c212: `give rise` had no
// argument slot for its `to`-PP, the PP fell to adjunct position, and an adjunct escaped a finite
// `that`-clause onto the matrix subject.
//
// This layer simulates the CORRECTED classification across the whole verb lexicon, so the real
// change can be measured WITHOUT a reseed — the change touches WordNet only, and UMLS is the
// 30-minute part of a reseed.
//
// BUILT BY DIFFING TWO IMPORTER RUNS, not by hand from the frame counts. That matters: `kinds` is
// a SET, so a synset carrying frames {2, 22} keeps its intransitive reading from frame 2 and
// merely GAINS the oblique slot. Of 1113 frame-22 synsets only 483 actually lose their
// intransitive; 877 gain an oblique-PP frame. Hand-writing this from the raw counts would have
// been wrong.
//
//   entries added      12000   (11940 oblique-PP, 60 intransitive from frame 23)
//   entries suppressed  6294   (6090 intransitive, 204 spurious oblique from frame 23)
//   axioms added         878
//
// Suppression works by redefining an entry with a non-matching `lexicon:form`: the lazy index
// skips an entry whose resolved form no longer normalizes to the queried key ("Shadow safety" in
// `dcg::lexicon`).
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
namespace core      = "urn:eigenius:core";
namespace epistemic = "urn:eigenius:reflection:epistemic";
namespace lexicon   = "urn:eigenius:lexicon";
namespace wn        = "urn:eigenius:wn";

